      'Additional Rules for Registered Persons Outside Business Activities',
      'FINRA requires registered persons to provide prompt written notice of any outside business activity to their employer. This includes any activity that involves compensation, including being a paid board member, working in a family business, or working part-time in a department store. An exclusion is doing charitable work without compensation. Firms may approve or disapprove of any outside business activity.\n\nPassive investments are exempt from this rule. A passive investment is one in which a person might invest or earn money through a business activity but plays no active role in its success. Income, if any, may be derived from dividends or royalties, but not a salary. For example, becoming a limited partner in a direct participation program is a passive investment, whereas working nights as a janitor is not.\n\nFidelity Bond Coverage\n\nEach member firm must maintain fidelity bond coverage on all employees to insure against loss due to employee theft or misappropriation of funds or securities. This does not cover market losses.',
