      'Record Retention Summary',
      'Record Retention Summary The time period for retention of records depends on the type of record.\n\nThe time period for retention of records depends on the type of record. Here is a summary of the ones that should be known for the exam: Three-year retention\n\nRetail communications:\n\n• Retail communications • Correspondence • Institutional communications e Advertising • Customer orders • Any other records not listed below\n\n• Correspondence\n• Institutional communications\n• Advertising\n\nCustomer orders\n\nAny other records not listed below Four-year retention\n\nWritten customer complaints Five-year retention\n\n• Anti-money laundering (AML) records (e.g., suspicious activity reports [SARs], currency transaction reports\n\n[CTRs|\n\n• Customer identification records\n\nSix-year retention\n\n• Customer account statements\n\nLifetime records of the firm\n\n• Articles of incorporation e Partnership articles (if a partnership) e Minutes of partners\' or directors\' meetings • Stock certificate books\n• Articles of incorporation\n\nPartnership articles (if a partnership) Minutes of partners\' or directors\' meetings Stock certificate books',
